;; min-fencei.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `min-fencei.s` (P2-SCALAR.6;
;; mirrored to rv64gc-lab-v0 at P4-SYSTEM.2 slice (f), RE-DERIVED at slice (g)).
;; Validate with:
;;   python3 scripts/check_sexp_schema.py min-fencei.expected.sexp schema/expectations.sexp

(comment "min-fencei.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `min-fencei.s`." "" "⛔ RE-DERIVATION (P4-SYSTEM.2 slice g, the mirror's fourth): the rv64i original is the retained" "minimized case of the cross-model divergence DIFF-FENCEI-EXECUTED — a difference id this unit" "does not record (rv64gc DECLARES Zifencei; the staged encoding leaves its slot UNBOUND, and" "this staging runs no cross-model comparison). The expect_divergence form is dropped with the" "reason recorded; the single semulith-side step is unchanged, and the slot-binding leaf" "re-derives this file to the legal fence.i when the slot binds.")
(expectations (program "min-fencei.s") (entry "0x80000000") (instructions 1) (step (n 0) (insn ".word 0x0000100F") (writes) (derivation "0x0000100F is fence.i. The staged encoding leaves the zifencei slot unbound, so the word matches no row of the generated decode table: a RESERVED instruction, whose behavior the architecture declares UNSPECIFIED. The laboratory's policy (D-RESERVED-DECODE) converts it to illegal-instruction with tval = the offending word (cause 0x02), delivered on this composition (zicsr's declared refinement); the expectations end at the delivered trap.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.5.2 (the reserved-instruction note: UNSPECIFIED) — decision D-RESERVED-DECODE")))
